## Re-syncing with upstream

The copy was taken from a working tree, so this repository shares no commits
with qm and `git merge` against it will not work without grafting. To compare
against upstream, clone qm separately and diff trees at the SHA above.

## What this copy does not yet include

`npm install` was run in the source tree before copying, so `package-lock.json`
may differ from qm's committed lock. Node modules were excluded.

`plugins/web-ui` has its own manifest and its dependencies are not vendored; one
of them (`xlsx`, fetched from cdn.sheetjs.com rather than the npm registry)
cannot be installed from behind a restricted egress proxy.
